Consider $abs(bold(x) - lambda bold(y))^2 >= 0$ for $lambda in RR$. Expanding,
$ abs(bold(x))^2 + lambda^2 abs(bold(y))^2 - 2 lambda bold(x) dot bold(y) >= 0 $
is a quadratic in $lambda$ that never becomes negative, so its discriminant is non-positive:
$ 4 (bold(x) dot bold(y))^2 - 4 abs(bold(x))^2 abs(bold(y))^2 <= 0. $
Rearranging gives $abs(bold(x) dot bold(y)) <= abs(bold(x)) abs(bold(y))$.
